# Intro: AREPO metal-advection comparison test

Reproduces Patrick Hirling's AREPO "Noctua" turbulent box test,
to compare metal transport against AREPO's moving-mesh result.

The run is non-cosmological with TimeIntegration:time_end set to the
physical time AREPO's run spanned. The AREPO run was cosmological.

# Configure
To run this example, configure with:
./configure --with-hydro=gizmo-mfv --with-riemann-solver=hllc --with-chemistry=GEAR_9 --with-cooling=none --with-feedback=none

Then,
make -j

You can also run this example with SPHENIX SPH, but note that does
not exchange mass between particles. To run with SPHENIX, configure with:
./configure --with-hydro=sphenix --with-chemistry=GEAR_9 --with-cooling=none --with-feedback=none

# Run
Type run.sh, and let's go!